# GHSA-4g2h-vm7x-747c / EEF-CVE-2026-28809 / esaml XXE
#
# The advisory is in esaml's own XML decoding (esaml_sp / esaml_util), which
# web-ng never calls. esaml is a direct dependency only for :xmerl_dsig
# signature verification, and every document it sees -- SAML responses and IdP
# metadata alike -- is parsed first by
# lib/serviceradar_web_ng_web/auth/saml_xml.ex with `dtd: :none`, which rejects
# any entity declaration and never fetches an external resource. Covered by
# test/phoenix/auth/saml_response_test.exs and saml_metadata_test.exs.
#
# There is no newer Hex release than esaml 4.6.0 available to upgrade to
# (re-verified 2026-09-25 via mix hex.info), so we track the advisory here until
# upstream publishes a patched package or the dependency is replaced.
GHSA-4g2h-vm7x-747c

# EEF-CVE-2026-93471 / esaml unbounded SAML message decompression
# EEF-CVE-2026-86696 / esaml atom creation from unsigned LogoutResponse status codes
# EEF-CVE-2026-105270 / esaml atom creation while parsing SAML messages
#
# All three are in esaml's own message decoding (its binding decoder, logout
# handling and parser). web-ng calls exactly one esaml function,
# :xmerl_dsig.verify, from lib/serviceradar_web_ng_web/auth/saml_response.ex;
# every SAML document is decoded and parsed by web-ng's own saml_xml.ex before
# that call, and web-ng has no SAML logout flow. scripts/elixir_dep_audit.sh
# fails if any other esaml module is ever called from web-ng, so this waiver
# cannot outlive the fact it rests on.
#
# No esaml release newer than 4.6.0 exists (re-verified 2026-10-22 via
# mix hex.info esaml; osv.dev lists no fixed version for any of the three).
EEF-CVE-2026-93471
EEF-CVE-2026-86696
EEF-CVE-2026-105270

